# Virtual environment

This repository uses a local virtual environment at **`.venv`** in the repo root. **Every test and pipeline program must run in that environment.**

- Before running **any** `python`, `pip`, `uv`, `pytest`, or package CLIs (`methyl-*`, etc.) in the terminal, activate from the repo root:

  `source .venv/bin/activate`

- When running shell commands for the user, use either activation as above or the equivalent explicit interpreter: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest ...` / `.venv/bin/methyl-centroid ...`.

- Prefer one-shot form when scripting: `source .venv/bin/activate && pytest ...`

- Do not assume system Python has project dependencies; validate tests and imports only inside `.venv`.
